{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#1953","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#1953","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#1953\",\"parent_revision\":\"14c9cc71ca46a75bdc35db5d6c2242c458bfc416a05202fba976b0d330bf6006\",\"root_revision\":\"14c9cc71ca46a75bdc35db5d6c2242c458bfc416a05202fba976b0d330bf6006\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: 2026-05-02\\n-->\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **add automatic backlink/inverse-cross-reference detection to research-cross-referencer agent** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Research entry: ./research/developer-tools/tolaria.md \u2014 pattern: Backlink detection via vault scan for wikilinks; neighborhood mode showing inverse relationships\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-04-26\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-04-26)\\n\\n### RT-ICA Assessment\\n\\n**Status: APPROVED-WITH-GAPS**\\n\\n| Input | Status | Source |\\n|-------|--------|--------|\\n| Functional intent | AVAILABLE | Item title is self-describing: detect when entry B is cited in entry A's Cross-References table, add a back-reference in entry B pointing to entry A |\\n| Agent boundary constraint | AVAILABLE | Agent file lines 119-130 defines what it cannot touch; backlink detection requires editing multiple files per run \u2014 conflicts with existing \\\"edit only the target research entry\\\" constraint |\\n| Cross-References section format | AVAILABLE | Agent file lines 49-66 documents table format |\\n| Existing vault state | AVAILABLE | 162+ entries, 20+ categories; no entries currently have a Cross-References section (verified by reading sample entries) |\\n| Trigger mechanism | MISSING | Not specified whether backlink detection runs within current single-entry invocation, as a separate post-pass, or both |\\n| Relationship description direction | MISSING | What text appears in entry B's Relationship column when the reference was authored from A's perspective is not defined |\\n\\n### Expected Behavior\\n\\nAfter research-cross-referencer adds a Cross-References entry in entry A pointing to entry B:\\n\\n- Entry B's Cross-References section also contains a row referencing entry A.\\n- The relationship description in entry B's row describes how entry A relates to entry B from B's perspective.\\n- If entry B had no Cross-References section before, one is created (appended after Freshness Tracking).\\n- If entry B already has a Cross-References row for entry A, no duplicate row is added.\\n- Entry A is unchanged by the backlink update to entry B.\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n1. After running research-cross-referencer on a new entry A that cites entries B and C, reading entry B contains a Cross-References row with a link to entry A.\\n2. After running research-cross-referencer on a new entry A that cites entries B and C, reading entry C contains a Cross-References row with a link to entry A.\\n3. If entry B already contained a Cross-References row for entry A before the run, re-running does not produce a duplicate row in entry B.\\n4. The Relationship column in entry B's backlink row describes how entry A relates to entry B from B's perspective \u2014 not a copy of entry A's relationship description.\\n5. The agent's return block reports BACKLINKS_UPDATED: N where N is the count of entries that received a new backlink row.\\n6. If entry B does not yet have a Cross-References section, one is created and appended after Freshness Tracking following the existing format.\\n7. The agent continues to not modify ./research/README.md (existing boundary constraint preserved).\\n\\n### Questions for Human\\n\\n- Should the backlink updates happen within the existing research-cross-referencer agent (requiring boundary relaxation), or should a new research-backlink-detector agent be created that runs as a post-pass?\\n- When writing entry B's backlink to entry A, should the agent (a) derive a new Relationship description from B's perspective, (b) reuse entry A's relationship description verbatim, or (c) use a generic \\\"referenced by {entry-A-name}\\\" label?\\n- Should backlink detection apply only to newly added cross-references from the current run (delta mode), or scan all existing Cross-References tables on every run (full scan mode)?\\n\\n### Resources\\n\\n| Type | Item |\\n|------|------|\\n| Agent | @research-cross-referencer \u2014 .claude/agents/research-cross-referencer.md |\\n| Agent | @research-curator |\\n| Prior work | .claude/agents/research-cross-referencer.md \u2014 Cross-References section format (lines 49-66), boundaries (lines 119-130) |\\n| Prior work | .claude/skills/research-curator/SKILL.md \u2014 orchestration skill |\\n| Prior work | research/README.md \u2014 162+ entry index |\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n\\n- Depends on: None \u2014 agent and research directory are both in place\\n- Blocks: None identified\\n\\n### Blockers\\n\\n- Trigger mechanism is unspecified: the current agent boundary states editing any file other than the target research entry is prohibited (agent file line 122). Implementing backlinks within the existing agent requires relaxing that boundary OR creating a separate agent for the backlink pass.\\n- Relationship description direction for backlinks is unspecified.\\n\\n### Effort\\n\\nMedium \u2014 The Cross-References section format, scoring logic, and README.md scan are already implemented in the agent. The new work is: after writing entry A's Cross-References table, iterate over each cited entry, read it, check whether a backlink to A exists, and write one if absent. Main complexity is deciding on the trigger model and handling the boundary constraint relaxation.\\n\\n<!-- artifact-gist:163ee3c197fbe863c6dae46b2dc1ca30 -->\\n\\n### Impact Radius\\n\\n| File | Change |\\n|------|--------|\\n| .claude/agents/research-cross-referencer.md | Relax \\\"edit only target entry\\\" boundary OR add new post-pass agent; add backlink write logic |\\n| All cited research entries (variable) | Receive new backlink rows when cited by other entries |\\n\\n### Story\\n\\nAs a researcher navigating the knowledge base, when I read an entry that is referenced by other entries, I want to see those back-references directly in the entry \u2014 so I can discover related work without manually scanning all 162+ entries for mentions of the current entry.\\n\\nAs the research-cross-referencer agent, when I add a cross-reference from entry A to entry B, I want entry B to automatically receive a reciprocal back-reference to entry A \u2014 so the knowledge graph stays bidirectionally consistent without requiring a separate manual pass.\\n\\n## Current State\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z-0</sub>\\n\\n`.claude/agents/research-cross-referencer.md` (referenced from research-curator/SKILL.md line 481) appends a Cross-References table to a target entry, but there is no inverse-link enforcement. When entry A is updated to cross-reference entry B, entry B does NOT automatically receive a corresponding back-reference to A. The cross-references graph is therefore directional and lossy \u2014 readers of B see only forward references it explicitly listed, never which entries point at it.\\n\\nThe Tolaria pattern detects backlinks dynamically by scanning the entire vault for wikilinks pointing at the current note. Research entries already contain Cross-References tables with paths in the form `[Resource Name](../category/filename.md)` \u2014 these are equivalent to wikilinks for backlink detection. No script in `.claude/skills/research-curator/scripts/` performs this scan; the validate_research.py validator does not check for asymmetric cross-references.\\n</div>\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z-1</sub>\\n\\n`.claude/agents/research-cross-referencer.md` (referenced from research-curator/SKILL.md line 481) appends a Cross-References table to a target entry, but there is no inverse-link enforcement. When entry A is updated to cross-reference entry B, entry B does NOT automatically receive a corresponding back-reference to A. The cross-references graph is therefore directional and lossy \u2014 readers of B see only forward references it explicitly listed, never which entries point at it.\\n\\nThe Tolaria pattern detects backlinks dynamically by scanning the entire vault for wikilinks pointing at the current note. Research entries already contain Cross-References tables with paths in the form `[Resource Name](../category/filename.md)` \u2014 these are equivalent to wikilinks for backlink detection. No script in `.claude/skills/research-curator/scripts/` performs this scan; the validate_research.py validator does not check for asymmetric cross-references.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Target State\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n`research-cross-referencer` agent (or a new `validate_research.py --check-backlinks` subcommand) walks every entry, parses the Cross-References tables, and builds an in-memory directed graph. For each edge A\u2192B with no reverse edge B\u2192A, the script emits a warning and either auto-appends the reverse row to B's Cross-References table (in `--fix` mode) or reports the asymmetry (in default mode).\\n\\nA `research_backlinks(path)` MCP tool (depends on the parent MCP server item) returns the list of entries that reference the given path.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Measurable Signal\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nRun `uv run .claude/skills/research-curator/scripts/validate_research.py --check-backlinks ./research/`. Output includes `asymmetric_cross_references: N` field with the count and a list of specific asymmetric pairs. Run with `--check-backlinks --fix` \u2014 second invocation reports `asymmetric_cross_references: 0`. Open any entry that was the target of a cross-reference; its Cross-References table now contains a row pointing back at the source entry.\\n\\nSource: Tolaria research entry (./research/developer-tools/tolaria.md), Relationship Navigation section \u2014 \\\"Backlink detection: Scans vault for notes referencing the current note via wikilinks. Neighborhood mode: Select an entity in the sidebar to explore outgoing relationships (grouped by type), inverse relationships, backlinks, and all connected notes in a single scrollable view.\\\"\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"162638cfddde5d72a94505149e171b39cf8d426013833568a3dc8bf3e025f4a3\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABVCcC8A\"}"}